// Arrival and leaving events play when the player walks into, travels to or
// walks out of a place. `chance`, `priority` and `cooldown` (in turns) control
// how often; a scene can check "player arrived by walking".

// The first visit to the clearing: Wren greets the player.
== event first_clearing_visit
name: Meeting Wren
found by: arriving at clearing
repeat: once
requires: quest lost_knife is not_started
play:
    A small woman by the lean-to looks up from her whittling. 'You must be the one in the cabin,' she says. 'I'm Wren.'

// Leaving the cabin at night: a moment at the door, then the player walks on.
// Without "~ continue moving" the player would stay where they are.
== event night_doorway
name: Into the dark
found by: leaving cabin east
repeat: always
requires: time is night
cooldown: 4
play:
    You pause in the doorway. The woods are very dark. [if player wears wool_coat]At least the coat is warm.[else]It's cold out there.[end if]
    * Go on
        ~ continue moving
    * Stay in
        You close the door again.

// An ending the player chooses. "~ ending <id>" ends the game; the id is shown
// as its title ("Left the woods"). This event comes up half the time
// (`chance`) and not again for 6 turns after (`cooldown`).
== event mist_beckons
name: The mist
found by: walking into old_bridge
repeat: always
chance: 50%
cooldown: 6
play:
    The mist on the far side of the bridge shifts, and for a moment you see a road beyond it, leading out of the woods.
    * Walk into the mist
        You cross the bridge without looking back. The woods grow quiet behind you, and then they are gone.
        ~ ending left_the_woods
    * Not today
        You stay where you are. The mist closes again.
